WEBVTT

00:16.980 --> 00:19.900
They look like chrysalises.
What do you think?

00:19.900 --> 00:21.650
I sense mana.

00:21.650 --> 00:24.110
It's similar to that chain
monster's, I think.

00:25.780 --> 00:27.280
I'll scout it out!

00:54.800 --> 00:55.940
Are you all right?!

00:57.570 --> 01:01.150
Y-You saved me. I was about to die...

01:02.650 --> 01:05.710
What are those things? Some sort of worm?

01:05.710 --> 01:10.530
The moment that eyeball looked at me,
I froze up and couldn't move.

01:10.530 --> 01:14.010
We can't just leave these here.
Let's fight at range.

01:14.010 --> 01:14.910
Got it!

01:14.910 --> 01:17.170
Guess that means this guy's up!

01:17.170 --> 01:19.250
Counting on you, Stinger Joe!

01:19.540 --> 01:20.990
What shall I do?

01:20.990 --> 01:22.360
Fire arrows, please.

01:22.360 --> 01:23.130
Right!

01:23.360 --> 01:25.590
Rain, use ice magic.

01:25.590 --> 01:29.440
They look like an insect's chrysalis,
so thermal changes might be effective.

01:29.440 --> 01:30.900
Got it.

01:31.350 --> 01:32.760
Physical Enchant!

01:32.760 --> 01:35.270
(Enhanced Arm Strength, Enhanced
Leg Strength, Enhanced Stamina)

01:35.630 --> 01:36.340
Ready?

01:36.340 --> 01:37.300
All set!

01:37.300 --> 01:38.370
I'm ready!

01:38.370 --> 01:39.310
All good.

01:39.310 --> 01:40.150
Yep!

01:40.150 --> 01:41.190
I'm going!

01:44.840 --> 01:46.070
Flash!

01:46.780 --> 01:48.490
(Flash)

01:51.030 --> 01:51.990
Blindness!

01:51.990 --> 01:53.740
(Blindness)

01:54.280 --> 01:56.250
Forbidden zone locked in ice...

01:56.250 --> 01:58.120
Here I go!

02:08.420 --> 02:10.480
Violently blow beneath the frozen star!

02:10.480 --> 02:13.810
Grade 5 Magic: Blizzard!

02:15.720 --> 02:16.720
(Blizzard)

02:26.980 --> 02:28.150
I couldn't finish it off.

02:28.150 --> 02:30.530
Not a problem! Magic Blade!

02:34.530 --> 02:35.910
Critical Weapon!

02:36.370 --> 02:37.410
(Critical Weapon)

02:50.050 --> 02:52.050
Okay, I think it's over.

03:03.150 --> 03:10.110
(I Left My A-Rank Party to Help My Former
Students Reach the Dungeon Depths)

04:24.980 --> 04:25.520
(Episode 12: The Golden Priestess)

04:25.520 --> 04:28.610
(Episode 12: The Golden Priestess)
And that gives us another ring.

04:28.610 --> 04:30.430
(Episode 12: The Golden Priestess)

04:30.430 --> 04:32.490
Are they dropping in place of magic gems?

04:33.840 --> 04:37.450
It does seem to be something this
dungeon's monsters have in common.

04:40.240 --> 04:41.150
What is it?

04:43.020 --> 04:43.830
Marina?

04:44.500 --> 04:46.810
Oh, right... Well...

04:50.440 --> 04:53.010
Give me a little time to
sort things out first.

04:53.570 --> 04:54.580
Okay.

04:57.130 --> 04:58.720
Let's rest over there for a bit.

04:59.310 --> 05:02.170
We're taking a little break.
Cut the stream.

05:02.170 --> 05:03.600
Goodnight.

05:06.820 --> 05:07.900
Smells nice.

05:08.360 --> 05:10.210
It's berry-flavored tea.

05:10.210 --> 05:12.180
It's not cheap, but...

05:12.180 --> 05:14.900
Ah, that sure hits the spot.

05:16.040 --> 05:17.990
The cookies are delicious, too.

05:18.320 --> 05:20.490
I'm glad you like them.

05:23.310 --> 05:26.500
So, um... Could I say something?

05:26.950 --> 05:28.430
Go for it.

05:28.430 --> 05:30.850
That monster earlier...

05:30.850 --> 05:33.250
It felt like I was fighting a human again.

05:33.570 --> 05:34.710
Yeah.

05:35.050 --> 05:37.530
But... that's not all.

05:38.770 --> 05:42.100
I cut through that pillar
on the rebound...

05:43.990 --> 05:47.140
and it felt like cutting
through a human then, too.

05:48.500 --> 05:54.030
Before, my Samurai job always
told me when I had cut a human.

05:56.360 --> 05:57.650
I wonder why...

05:58.450 --> 06:01.840
Want to cut something else
around here to test it?

06:01.840 --> 06:06.410
No, actually, I already tried
that in the next room over.

06:06.410 --> 06:09.260
I still couldn't be sure, though.

06:09.260 --> 06:12.620
I think it's because the Samurai
part of me isn't fully mature yet.

06:12.620 --> 06:16.420
I only seem to feel it when
there's a life at stake.

06:16.840 --> 06:20.470
Sorry for saying all this weird stuff.

06:20.470 --> 06:23.630
Thanks for telling us, Marina.

06:24.660 --> 06:25.930
Yuke...

06:26.360 --> 06:29.590
There is definitely something
strange about this dungeon.

06:29.590 --> 06:31.720
Even the spirits feel off.

06:31.720 --> 06:32.360
How?

06:32.360 --> 06:36.000
There's a subtle inconsistency
in my communications with them.

06:36.000 --> 06:40.790
It's like speaking in gestures to someone
who doesn't understand words.

06:40.790 --> 06:43.360
Like the answers they give don't match up.

06:45.390 --> 06:46.620
If I had to describe it,

06:47.140 --> 06:49.700
it's similar to the Grey Field.

06:50.160 --> 06:51.920
The place where Persephone was?

06:52.720 --> 06:54.250
I get what you mean.

06:54.600 --> 06:57.000
The mana in this dungeon
is different, too.

06:57.000 --> 06:59.760
The air isn't the same as
it is in normal places.

06:59.760 --> 07:02.760
I feel that, too. On a physical level.

07:03.080 --> 07:05.140
What should we do, Master?

07:06.060 --> 07:07.620
Let's go up to the roof.

07:07.620 --> 07:10.390
I want to get a view of the whole city.

07:10.700 --> 07:11.880
Zoom!

07:12.650 --> 07:13.790
It's huge...

07:13.790 --> 07:16.760
About as big as Duna, if not bigger.

07:16.760 --> 07:20.650
It's hard to believe
all this is a dungeon.

07:20.910 --> 07:24.720
Yeah. So this is Glad Shi-im...

07:24.720 --> 07:27.030
I've committed everything in view
to memory.

07:27.030 --> 07:29.790
Okay, then, let's head to the castle.

07:30.390 --> 07:33.040
Once we verify what it looks
like inside the castle...

07:33.670 --> 07:35.080
we'll leave for the day.

07:37.300 --> 07:40.270
It's too quiet. It seems unnatural.

07:40.270 --> 07:41.980
You said it.

07:41.980 --> 07:44.990
Loge said there were other people here.

07:44.990 --> 07:48.010
Where is that old guy now, anyway?

07:48.350 --> 07:50.830
He didn't show up on our stream.

07:50.830 --> 07:54.610
It's possible we really
were hallucinating.

07:54.610 --> 07:58.600
You think so? But you saw
him too, didn't you, Rain?

07:58.600 --> 07:59.280
Yeah.

07:59.850 --> 08:03.480
Since I have this Sanity Ring
Yuke gave me,

08:03.480 --> 08:05.280
mental interference doesn't affect me.

08:05.660 --> 08:09.040
So that old man definitely exists.

08:09.400 --> 08:14.660
Which means it might be natural
to conclude that the Camerat is under

08:14.660 --> 08:16.290
some sort of outside influence.

08:16.580 --> 08:17.790
That's true.

08:20.280 --> 08:22.050
Yuke, over there.

08:28.090 --> 08:29.220
Loge!

08:32.560 --> 08:35.230
Welcome to Vordan Castle.

08:35.230 --> 08:38.730
Tell me, Loge. What is this city?

08:39.960 --> 08:42.480
And what would you do with that knowledge?

08:42.480 --> 08:45.610
This town stained by the
twilight and its people

08:45.610 --> 08:50.180
are already saved so well
that they are beyond saving.

08:50.870 --> 08:54.000
Were those monsters originally humans?

08:54.000 --> 08:59.010
Well, now! Just what is a human, then?

08:59.010 --> 09:04.010
Is it a creature with four
limbs and a head? Or is it—

09:04.010 --> 09:06.720
That's not what I'm asking you.

09:06.720 --> 09:08.550
You know that, don't you?

09:08.550 --> 09:10.170
Oh, no, Mr. Yuke.

09:10.170 --> 09:15.020
Whether a thing can be a
human regardless of its form

09:15.020 --> 09:18.270
is a critically important detail.

09:18.600 --> 09:21.400
Loge, what are the golden rings?

09:21.400 --> 09:26.280
The ring is an item we call the One Gold.

09:26.280 --> 09:29.540
"One"? But there are many of them.

09:29.540 --> 09:31.760
What are you compiling with them?

09:31.760 --> 09:32.910
Compiling?

09:33.400 --> 09:37.380
Wisdom does not necessarily
bring happiness,

09:37.380 --> 09:40.540
little lady with the sky-blue hair.

09:40.910 --> 09:45.050
I just want to know.
What do those rings do?

09:45.050 --> 09:48.340
I believe you are already aware.

09:48.340 --> 09:49.590
Old man?!

09:50.280 --> 09:53.530
When might we meet again?

09:53.530 --> 09:57.600
I, Loge, shall look forward
to that moment.

09:57.600 --> 10:00.730
Will you answer our questions then?!

10:00.730 --> 10:05.060
Let the truth find you on its own!

10:05.740 --> 10:08.620
Just who is that man, exactly?

10:08.620 --> 10:09.990
I don't know...

10:12.560 --> 10:14.920
But it looks like we've been invited in.

10:14.920 --> 10:19.340
Okay, let's take a look around
inside and then head back.

10:20.540 --> 10:25.000
Entering Vordan Castle.
Let's have fun, but be careful.

10:27.280 --> 10:29.260
How'd that data analysis turn out?

10:29.260 --> 10:31.510
I'm rushing through it right now.

10:31.960 --> 10:36.040
We've scoped out the general layout of
the structure he called Vordan Castle.

10:36.040 --> 10:39.330
It has a garden,
a training ground, stables...

10:39.330 --> 10:43.520
But we were unable to find
a way to sneak inside.

10:43.520 --> 10:47.790
The old guy you called Loge didn't
show up on the stream again,

10:47.790 --> 10:50.660
but it doesn't seem to have
been a group hallucination.

10:51.000 --> 10:53.350
Do you think it could be
some kind of magic?

10:53.350 --> 10:57.640
Well, in any case, the investigation
is going fantastically.

10:57.640 --> 11:00.450
Your logs are put together well.

11:00.450 --> 11:02.170
You're doing fine work for us.

11:02.660 --> 11:06.050
(Royal Academy Local Supervisor, Viscount Bodeman)
The academy thanks you as well, Yuke.

11:06.340 --> 11:09.160
Oh, I'm just glad I could be of help.

11:09.160 --> 11:13.550
I wasn't expecting you to appear
here in person, Viscount Bodeman.

11:14.050 --> 11:18.250
I wanted to see this bizarre
dungeon with my own eyes.

11:18.250 --> 11:21.160
Now, there's no need to worry.

11:21.160 --> 11:24.220
We are on the side of adventurers.

11:24.220 --> 11:30.010
Most of my knowledge of
dungeons came from your writings!

11:30.010 --> 11:31.820
I can never fully express my respect.

11:32.120 --> 11:35.600
I'm glad to have been of use in the field.

11:35.600 --> 11:37.950
Now, as for this dungeon...

11:38.610 --> 11:42.260
It's possible that it limits entry.

11:42.260 --> 11:43.710
Will it be designated as sealed?

11:44.620 --> 11:47.960
And as for the monster materials
you brought back...

11:47.960 --> 11:49.840
The examination is complete.

11:50.790 --> 11:52.970
Results of material appraisal...

11:52.970 --> 11:56.520
"Derived from human or similar being."

11:57.170 --> 11:58.470
So we were right.

11:58.820 --> 12:01.410
Hmm? You knew?

12:01.410 --> 12:04.810
One of our members has the Samurai job,

12:04.810 --> 12:07.840
and she said it felt like she
was cutting through a human.

12:07.840 --> 12:10.350
Assuming all the monsters
that appear there,

12:10.350 --> 12:14.720
including the Chain Man and
chrysalises, are human,

12:14.720 --> 12:17.990
we can no longer allow ordinary
adventurers to enter.

12:18.610 --> 12:19.990
I'm sure you can't.

12:19.990 --> 12:23.180
If we let ordinary folks go in there,

12:23.180 --> 12:27.080
we'd just be asking for more extensive
damages or even an Overflow.

12:28.600 --> 12:32.940
It sounds like we were
in a very risky place.

12:32.940 --> 12:37.810
Viscount, Maniella, is this
what Marina was talking about?

12:43.630 --> 12:47.560
She said that even cutting the
pillar felt like cutting a human?

12:47.560 --> 12:50.050
Is that even possible?

12:50.840 --> 12:54.990
I brought back bits of the ground and
buildings from inside the dungeon.

12:54.990 --> 12:57.630
They should have been
received yesterday...

12:57.630 --> 12:58.630
Hey!

12:58.630 --> 12:59.740
Y-Yes, ma'am?

12:59.740 --> 13:03.400
You got some boards and rocks
and stuff from this boy, right?

13:03.400 --> 13:05.410
Were the appraisals on those done?

13:05.410 --> 13:09.480
No, I've been told the official
appraisal will be completed tomorrow.

13:09.480 --> 13:12.820
Well, go smack that appraiser in the
butt and wake him up right now!

13:12.820 --> 13:13.990
On the double!

13:13.990 --> 13:15.510
Y-Yes, ma'am!

13:15.510 --> 13:16.520
I swear...

13:16.520 --> 13:19.150
Also, what about those golden rings?

13:19.150 --> 13:24.990
Yes, we've already begun production
on the material Rain requested.

13:24.990 --> 13:26.140
Thank you.

13:26.630 --> 13:30.420
There is one other important
thing I must tell you.

13:30.420 --> 13:32.400
You know what happened to Misty, right?

13:32.400 --> 13:35.900
I know they stepped down from the
mission because they felt unwell.

13:36.450 --> 13:41.910
It seems some of the people watching their
stream experienced similar effects.

13:41.910 --> 13:42.910
Huh?

13:43.320 --> 13:49.160
There were several cases, ranging from
mild illness to sudden violent outbursts.

13:49.160 --> 13:52.420
It's probably safe to assume
there's something in that stream.

13:52.710 --> 13:55.550
Could it have been that light after all?

13:55.550 --> 13:58.930
It might have some kind of
effect on people's minds.

13:59.220 --> 14:02.750
This town stained by the
twilight and its people

14:02.750 --> 14:07.060
are already saved so well
that they are beyond saving.

14:09.060 --> 14:11.970
We intend to put the
investigation on hold for now

14:11.970 --> 14:17.070
and have the government decide whether
the dungeon should be sealed or not.

14:17.070 --> 14:18.530
All right.

14:18.530 --> 14:21.040
What should Clover do?

14:21.040 --> 14:25.340
We may have you go in to
investigate a few more times,

14:25.340 --> 14:28.400
so I'd like you to stay in Duna
for a while.

14:28.400 --> 14:31.510
I've already talked to the Singing Fawn.

14:31.510 --> 14:32.080
Okay.

14:32.590 --> 14:35.340
We'll head back to Duna then.

14:38.190 --> 14:39.880
Th-This is terrible!

14:39.880 --> 14:42.170
That girl went all weird!

14:42.170 --> 14:42.850
Weird?

14:42.850 --> 14:45.890
Yeah, like... she lit up!

14:54.960 --> 14:57.640
S-So... is she okay?

14:57.640 --> 14:58.680
What happened?

14:58.680 --> 15:02.070
I don't know.
She just... suddenly did this.

15:02.070 --> 15:03.990
Nothing in particular triggered it.

15:04.820 --> 15:08.000
I've been waiting for you, Yuke Feldio.

15:08.600 --> 15:10.120
Who are you?

15:10.470 --> 15:13.880
I was once known as the Golden Priestess.

15:14.440 --> 15:15.750
Golden Priestess?

15:17.000 --> 15:20.440
There is little time remaining.

15:20.440 --> 15:25.260
The world you live in is in
danger of facing a culling.

15:25.750 --> 15:27.070
What do you mean?

15:27.070 --> 15:28.570
What's a "culling"?

15:28.570 --> 15:31.020
It means removing things
that are not needed.

15:31.580 --> 15:34.320
Now that our world has
begun to show through,

15:34.320 --> 15:36.610
it will likely destroy you all.

15:38.750 --> 15:41.570
You saw Glad Shi-im, did you not?

15:42.150 --> 15:46.360
Twilight, distortion, and
a bloated consciousness

15:46.360 --> 15:49.160
will one day blanket this entire world.

15:49.600 --> 15:52.630
Twilight? Do you mean that light?

15:52.630 --> 15:54.400
The light of the setting sun.

15:54.400 --> 15:58.380
It is the cause of the distortion
and the essence of the culling.

15:58.760 --> 16:01.240
I knew it was something bad.

16:01.240 --> 16:04.180
It's clear that light swallowed Misty.

16:04.680 --> 16:06.890
So we'll be swallowed by it, too?

16:07.210 --> 16:11.020
You have already crossed the
border between worlds once.

16:11.020 --> 16:12.580
You mean...

16:12.580 --> 16:13.890
How do you know?

16:14.340 --> 16:16.650
You have deep ties with the twilight.

16:19.280 --> 16:22.990
So long as you avoid going too deep,
it is unlikely to swallow you.

16:24.760 --> 16:26.690
Seek out Loge.

16:26.690 --> 16:29.010
He knows all there is to know.

16:29.010 --> 16:30.910
That old guy?

16:30.910 --> 16:34.460
We've met him a few times, but
he won't tell us anything.

16:34.460 --> 16:36.220
You must make him speak.

16:36.220 --> 16:42.090
He remains on the very edge of
normalcy by distorting himself.

16:42.370 --> 16:45.050
Why are you telling us this?

16:45.050 --> 16:46.970
We should have fallen.

16:46.970 --> 16:51.970
All of us, the foolish king,
and his unknown people.

16:51.970 --> 16:55.060
But we could not accept our collapse.

16:55.860 --> 16:59.570
And then we wished for our
eternity to be golden.

16:59.570 --> 17:00.860
Golden?

17:01.170 --> 17:03.450
That which no human should touch,

17:03.450 --> 17:05.320
the cursed universal vessel,

17:05.320 --> 17:09.740
the fruit of the World Tree
that grants all wishes.

17:09.740 --> 17:11.560
Wishes?

17:11.560 --> 17:15.000
What kind of wish created that weird city?

17:15.310 --> 17:21.120
Yuke Feldio, stop the Twilight King
and destroy the gold.

17:21.650 --> 17:27.780
Should you fail, this world will be
swallowed by the twilight as well.

17:27.780 --> 17:30.850
Please, take our sin from us.

17:37.760 --> 17:38.800
Are you okay?

17:39.330 --> 17:41.110
Yes... I'm fine.

17:41.110 --> 17:43.610
Your voice and expression
are totally different!

17:44.920 --> 17:49.990
Um... Once again...
I'm pleased to meet you.

17:49.990 --> 17:53.730
I'm glad you woke up, um...

17:53.730 --> 17:55.000
I'm Niberune.

17:55.000 --> 17:56.680
Okay, "Rune" it is!

17:56.680 --> 17:57.850
Rune?

17:57.850 --> 18:00.640
Are you feeling all right, Rune?

18:01.580 --> 18:02.630
I suppose so.

18:03.240 --> 18:05.740
The divine aura she had is gone.

18:05.740 --> 18:09.720
But the presence of the
twilight is still there.

18:09.720 --> 18:14.090
So should we assume she's
connected to that city?

18:14.090 --> 18:15.520
I guess that's obvious, huh?

18:15.900 --> 18:20.740
Um... Niberune, do you
remember what just happened?

18:20.740 --> 18:22.600
Yes, a bit.

18:22.600 --> 18:25.530
But that wasn't actually me.

18:25.530 --> 18:29.220
She's a fragment of someone
who resides within me,

18:29.220 --> 18:30.910
and she's gone now.

18:31.150 --> 18:34.970
I see. You don't need to worry about that.

18:36.170 --> 18:37.910
If all this is true,

18:38.390 --> 18:39.980
it's a big deal.

18:40.500 --> 18:45.420
Something far greater than ordinary
adventurers like us can handle.

18:45.420 --> 18:49.810
(One Week Later)

18:49.810 --> 18:53.700
Forgive me, but could you
leave Yuke and me alone?

18:53.700 --> 18:57.060
Why? You saying an old lady
would just be in the way?

18:57.060 --> 18:59.900
Fine, fine. Upsie-daisy.

19:01.310 --> 19:02.480
(Royal Academy Director, Marquis Bedibore)

19:02.480 --> 19:04.820
(Royal Academy Director, Marquis Bedibore)
You needn't be so nervous.

19:04.820 --> 19:07.320
O-Of course I'm nervous.

19:07.320 --> 19:11.950
I had no idea that not only the viscount
was here, but the academy director, too.

19:12.210 --> 19:15.560
Yes, I received Bodeman's report.

19:15.560 --> 19:17.880
That's why I hurried out here.

19:17.880 --> 19:20.330
You called it a "culling," correct?

19:20.740 --> 19:22.500
Yes, Marquis.

19:22.500 --> 19:24.710
Um, may I ask a question?

19:24.710 --> 19:26.120
Of course.

19:26.120 --> 19:29.970
You needn't concern yourself
with my status at the moment.

19:29.970 --> 19:31.700
What is a culling?

19:33.150 --> 19:35.290
I suppose you ought to know.

19:35.790 --> 19:38.510
You are the one who was chosen, after all.

19:38.510 --> 19:39.350
Chosen?

19:41.430 --> 19:44.280
This is a visual of an old mural in
the basement of the royal household.

19:46.090 --> 19:51.560
The former academy director—my
father—was researching this.

19:54.710 --> 19:55.870
Can you read it?

19:56.120 --> 19:58.940
No, I can't read ancient script.

19:58.940 --> 20:03.210
According to my father, the culling
is a worldwide screening.

20:03.210 --> 20:04.590
A screening?

20:04.590 --> 20:10.130
Yes. Did you know there are hints as
to the existence of parallel worlds?

20:10.130 --> 20:13.260
I felt that when I was
in Achromatic Darkness.

20:13.640 --> 20:18.490
Our world and parallel worlds
generally do not coexist,

20:18.970 --> 20:22.640
but at times, they attempt to overlap.

20:23.340 --> 20:27.430
The large-scale event that occurs to
determine which world will remain

20:27.430 --> 20:29.150
is known as a culling.

20:29.650 --> 20:35.020
But from what I've heard about all this,
it seems to be arbitrary in this case.

20:35.610 --> 20:39.160
I believe it is not something our
world brought upon itself,

20:39.160 --> 20:43.160
but rather, was forced upon it by
the so-called Twilight City.

20:43.840 --> 20:45.660
When Niberune spoke of it,

20:45.660 --> 20:49.920
it sounded as if it was brought
into this world by accident.

20:54.280 --> 20:57.880
In any case, the culling is upon us.

20:57.880 --> 21:00.390
I will have to rely on you to handle this.

21:00.630 --> 21:01.770
Excuse me?

21:02.090 --> 21:06.000
It is said that some form of
countermeasure will be enacted

21:06.000 --> 21:09.120
to defend our world in
response to the culling.

21:09.580 --> 21:10.900
Behold.

21:14.650 --> 21:15.800
This is the hero.

21:16.690 --> 21:18.160
Don't tell me...

21:18.800 --> 21:21.330
Yes. Yuke Feldio,

21:21.330 --> 21:25.090
you will become the hero
and save this world!

22:56.000 --> 22:56.640
(Biblion, the Book Spirit)

22:56.640 --> 22:59.630
(Biblion, the Book Spirit)
Next time, "Biblion, the Book Spirit."

22:59.630 --> 23:01.010
(Biblion, the Book Spirit)
